CORE
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ initialized: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ assigned and incremented: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ through its address: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ lvalue: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The resolver substituted the initializer of every variable template
specialization, so counter<char> was the prvalue 3 ("assignment error: '3'
not an lvalue").  Only specializations usable in constant expressions
(constexpr or const) are substituted now.  Found while diagnosing
cpp20_range_adaptor_closure_invoked_through_invoke_impl.
